{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.signflip_requires_diagonal_cross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.signflip_requires_diagonal_cross","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L189-L198","doc":"**The sign flip forces a diagonal crossing (surviving necessary\ncondition).** If `familyIm` is positive at one substrate point and negative\nat another, the two `u`-values lie in OPPOSITE regions relative to the\ndiagonal `|Re u| = |Im u|`: `|Im u₁| < |Re u₁|` but `|Re u₂| < |Im u₂|`. So\nany `u(q₀)` realizing the measured flip must CROSS that diagonal between the\nanchors. Via `FigureEightComplexVolume.signflip_forces_diagonal_cross`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.transverse_const_family_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.transverse_const_family_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L173-L185","doc":"**F3 exclusion (the #3773 survivor, refuted against the corrected form).**\nWith both anchors in the small-excursion regime `(a·dᵢ)² < c₀²` both family\nvalues are negative (same sign), contradicting one positive and one negative\nanchor value: F3 CANNOT reproduce the measured `S(muon) > 0 > S(proton)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.transverse_const_product_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.transverse_const_product_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L165-L171","doc":"The transverse-constant family's cross-anchor product is POSITIVE when both\nanchors stay inside the small-excursion regime (both values negative) —\nsame sign, no flip. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.transverse_const_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.transverse_const_neg","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L157-L163","doc":"Within `(a·d)² < c₀²` the transverse-constant family value is NEGATIVE:\n`familyIm(a·d, c₀) = (√3/4)((a·d)² − c₀²) < 0`. Reuses\n`FigureEightComplexVolume.f3_re_linear_same_sign`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.phase_crossing_family_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.phase_crossing_family_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L137-L149","doc":"**F2 exclusion.** The minimal phase-crossing family cannot reproduce the\nsign flip near `q*`: with both anchors in the small-excursion regime the\ncross-anchor product is `≥ 0`, contradicting one positive and one negative\nanchor value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.phase_crossing_product_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.phase_crossing_product_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L129-L135","doc":"The phase-crossing family's cross-anchor product is non-negative when both\nanchors stay inside the small-excursion regime — same sign, no flip. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.phase_crossing_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.phase_crossing_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L118-L127","doc":"Within the small excursion `b²d² ≤ a²`, the phase-crossing family value is\nnon-negative: `familyIm(a·d, b·d²) = (√3/4)·d²·(a² − b²d²) ≥ 0`. The old\n`cubic_ratio_law` (`∝ d³`) was a wrong-form artefact; the corrected leading\nbehaviour is `∝ d²`, even in `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.fixed_phase_family_excluded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.fixed_phase_family_excluded","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L103-L114","doc":"**F1 exclusion (structural, sign invariant).** A fixed-phase leading-order\nfamily cannot reproduce a sign flip: if `S` agrees with the family and\ntakes a positive and a negative value, contradiction. The measured\n`S(muon) > 0 > S(proton)` therefore excludes the family. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.fixed_phase_product_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.fixed_phase_product_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L93-L101","doc":"The fixed-phase family's product across any two substrate points is a\nperfect square — the sign of `familyIm` is the SAME on both sides of `q*`.\n`familyIm(cx·d, cy·d) = (√3/4)(cx² − cy²)d²`, even in `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.familyIm_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.familyIm_eq","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L83-L89","doc":"The corrected leading form: `familyIm x y = (√3/4)(x² − y²)` — a HARMONIC\nquadratic form (vanishing on the diagonals `|x| = |y|`), NOT the earlier\n`√3·x·y`. Direct from `imV₄₁`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.familyIm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.UDeformFamilyPruning.familyIm","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/UDeformFamilyPruning.lean#L76-L81","doc":"The family's imaginary part: the deformed complex volume's Chern–Simons\npart evaluated on the two real components `(x, y)` of the deformation,\n`familyIm x y = (𝔙₄₁⟨x, y⟩).im`. Its identification with the concrete\nfigure-eight complex volume is `QOU.Knot.FigureEightComplexVolume.V₄₁`,\nnot a fresh Lean claim. ","signatureChunk":0}]}